1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,897
Wolfgang Reviewer The

2
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:01,810
second one

3
00:00:01,893 --> 00:00:07,980
is

4
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,050
Iron

5
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:19,963
Man.

6
00:00:20,046 --> 00:00:22,380
I think that is near
the end of the journey!

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,040
THE END

8
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:23,210
Let's go.

9
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,760
The End

10
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:23,860
Thank you.

11
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,280
Oh, my God.

12
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,720
What is that, a helicopter?

13
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,440
It's Speedwagon Foundation.

14
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:22,064
They're looking for a
solid place to touch down.

15
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:24,020
Speed Wagon Foundation?

16
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:28,377
They're your associates that are taking
care of Mom in Japan, right, old man?

17
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:29,290
You're kidding.

18
00:06:29,373 --> 00:06:31,634
We're gonna have to ride in that thing?

19
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:37,177
No, I wish we could
hitch a ride with them.

20
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,554
But those young men aren't stand users.

21
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,857
If the enemy should attack us,
we'd end up involving them.

22
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,999
Then what is that helicopter
doing here, Jostar-san?

23
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,310
Hmm.

24
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,598
I've requested they bring in backup.

25
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:50,970
A backup?

26
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,357
He's got a bit of an attitude problem,

27
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:10,937
so it took a lot of hard
work to get him here.

28
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:11,850
Mr.

29
00:07:11,933 --> 00:07:14,957
Joestar, it is not possible for
him to accompany us on this trip.

30
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,380
He cannot back us up.

31
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,858
Sounds like you know him, Avdor-san.

32
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:24,210
Him.

33
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:25,940
Oh, yes.

34
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:32,130
Wait a minute.

35
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:36,484
If he's going to back us up, then
he must be a stand user, right?

36
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:40,620
Yes, and this stand user is represented
by the tarot card, The Fool.

37
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:52,977
The fool or do you mean the idiot?

38
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:57,120
Sounds like his card might
be lacking a little upstairs.

39
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,817
You will be glad he is not your enemy!

40
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,557
You would never beat him, huh?

41
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:04,080
What did you just say?

42
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:07,620
You got a lot of nerve
talking to me like that.

43
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,960
It is the truth.

44
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:10,737
Now take your hands off me.

45
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:11,937
Knock it off, Victor.

46
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:14,314
It looks like the helicopter's landing.

47
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,250
Mr.

48
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:49,557
Joestar, we're glad to
see you're doing well.

49
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,137
Thank you for your trouble.

50
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:52,280
I appreciate it.

51
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,440
Which one of you guys is the stand user?

52
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:15,920
Well, which one of you is it?

53
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:17,370
Huh?

54
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,795
Well, it's actually neither one of us.

55
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,660
He's here in the back seat.

56
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,150
Where?

57
00:09:34,233 --> 00:09:35,063
It's empty.

58
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,600
Yeah, he's there.

59
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:42,500
What, huh? Who, huh? Where?

60
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:44,170
What?

61
00:09:44,253 --> 00:09:45,083
Is he a shrimp?

62
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,500
Come out of here!

63
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,760
Whoa, watch out! Be careful.

64
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,437
He's in a really bad mood.

65
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,297
The ride over was pretty rough.

66
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:53,280
What's this?

67
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,400
I told you he has an attitude problem.

68
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:59,300
Now step back, Polnareff.

69
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:12,920
A dog?

70
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,720
Old man, this can't be.

71
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,680
Yes, this dog is the
stand user of the pool.

72
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:23,000
His name is Iggy, and he loves
to pull and chew on human hair.

73
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,337
Nobody knows where he came from,

74
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:29,797
and when the animal control officers
in New York weren't able to catch him,

75
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,233
Avdol was called in to get the job done.

76
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:37,360
Oh, and yes, when Iggy chews on a
person's hair, he has a tendency to fart.

77
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:40,320
It's a nasty habit.

78
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,540
Get off, you damn dog!

79
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,560
I'll teach you a lesson!

80
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:53,881
Shut the air up!

81
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:13,820
What?

82
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,720
What's this? Wow!

83
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,440
I can't cut it!

84
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:34,677
To put it simply it is a
stand of the sand they say

85
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,717
simplicity is power i'm not
sure i could beat him either.

86
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:42,557
hey help me get rid of this damn dog

87
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:45,137
do you have some of his favorite treats?

88
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:48,867
Yep, there's no way we could
have brought him here without it.

89
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:56,040
Hey, don't let him see the box!

90
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:09,180
He has a big weakness for
coffee-flavored chewing gum.

91
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:13,100
But Iggy is the type who will
never allow himself to be tamed.

92
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:14,397
What a pain.

93
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,537
At least take off the wrapper first.

94
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:19,149
How is a dog supposed
to serve as a backup?

95
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:03,650
Interesting.

96
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:05,760
A dog who's a stand user.

97
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,477
Here's the food and water you'll
need for the rest of the trip.

98
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,757
These other crates contain medical
supplies and extra clothes.

99
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,670
Thank you.

100
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:44,324
Before you leave, I'd
like to ask you one thing.

101
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,310
It's about...

102
00:13:45,393 --> 00:13:46,700
it's about my daughter.

103
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,820
How is Holly's medical condition?

104
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,581
Don't hold anything back from me.

105
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,820
Well, I'm afraid I have some bad news.

106
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,540
She's not doing very well.

107
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:04,917
Your daughter's rapidly losing strength,
and her life is still in grave danger.

108
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,977
According to the prognosis of
the Foundation's physicians,

109
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:10,180
at best, she has two more weeks.

110
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,020
I see.

111
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,940
We don't have time!

112
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,700
Damn it.

113
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:41,900
Only two weeks left, huh?

114
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,260
What a pain this is.

115
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:20,060
I don't know.

116
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:03,917
Now why is this shitty mud
allowed to be on the seat,

117
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,657
and we have to plant our
asses on the bed of the truck?

118
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:08,340
My butt is killing me!

119
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:14,109
Let's just wait until
the gum loses flavor.

120
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,249
As soon as it grows stale,

121
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:21,125
lure him to the back of the truck with a
new piece of gum and then grab the seat.

122
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,480
God damn you, dog!

123
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:44,937
Hey, old man.

124
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:45,900
What's that?

125
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:57,154
Say, that is in the direction
the helicopter was headed.

126
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,940
No sign of any damage from weapons.

127
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:35,520
It's almost like it just slammed into
the ground. An accident? Be careful.

128
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:39,662
It's quite possible this could be
an attack from an enemy's stand.

129
00:17:56,980 --> 00:18:01,060
Over here, it's the pilot. He's dead.

130
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:06,956
Be careful with him.

131
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:08,865
You never know what's lurking.

132
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:13,380
There's scratch marks on the fuselage.

133
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,330
Water?

134
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,400
A ton of water.

135
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,180
From his mouth.

136
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,380
No, from his lungs.

137
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,190
Impossible!

138
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:47,440
What the hell is going on?

139
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:51,427
This guy drowned in the
middle of the desert!

140
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,280
But how?

141
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,350
Hey!

142
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,675
Here's the other one!

143
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:13,880
Are you all right?

144
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,020
Don't move him.

145
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,000
What happened here?

146
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:21,430
Water.

147
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:24,570
Mr.

148
00:19:24,653 --> 00:19:26,160
Joestar, here, take this.

149
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:27,781
Here, my friend.

150
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,880
It's water. Drink it.

151
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:35,900
No! No!

152
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:38,160
The water!

153
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,960
It's attacking me!

154
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,040
Ah-ha-ha!

155
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,097
Ah-ha-ha!

156
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,450
Ah-ha-ha-ha!

157
00:19:50,580 --> 00:19:52,060
It's an enemy stand!

158
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:11,220
The enemy's stand is hiding
inside the canteen. Damn it.

159
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:15,517
What's to be gained by attacking those
innocent men from Speedwagon Foundation?

160
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,157
Avdol, did you see what
kind of stand it was?

161
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,920
All I saw was the hand, but it
is still inside the canteen.

162
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,540
I have not seen it come out of there yet.

163
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:27,512
Jotaro, search for the enemy's main body.

164
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:30,520
I'm searching for it now.

165
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:48,180
I can't see the main body anywhere.

166
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:50,290
There.

167
00:20:50,373 --> 00:20:51,817
Looks like he's controlling
it from a distance,

168
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:54,194
and the stand seems to be pretty small.

169
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,720
Polnareff, attack the canteen. What?

170
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:00,980
You're asking me?

171
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:04,317
Were you even here when the
entire head of the pilot

172
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:07,224
got sucked through the
tiny hole of the canteen?

173
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:10,782
If I puncture any holes
in that thing, who knows?

174
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:12,920
No way!

175
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,357
You're closer to it!

176
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:18,377
Why don't you just use your emerald
splash and blow it the hell out of here?

177
00:21:18,460 --> 00:21:20,166
I don't want to do it either.

178
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:23,737
Don't try to get me to do
what you don't want to do.

179
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,349
What kind of twisted
mind do you have, huh?

180
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:33,770
What the...

181
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,260
It got Kakyoin!

182
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:51,840
It got Kakyoin!

183
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:54,440
Ah, Kakyoin! Kakyoin!

184
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,840
It got his eyes!

185
00:21:57,820 --> 00:21:59,360
Polareff, don't panic.

186
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:02,129
Use Chariot to protect
yourself in Kakyoin.

187
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:13,420
He's gonna lose!

188
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,080
What's going on?

189
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:39,037
Why would it bother to
attack the pilot's dead body?

190
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:40,400
No, that's not it.

191
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:42,117
It didn't go after the body.

192
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:44,553
It went after the watch's alarm instead.

193
00:22:45,060 --> 00:22:46,160
The alarm.

194
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:49,020
Then it uses sound to find its targets.

195
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:02,520
Run for the truck, Baldoref!

196
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:20,480
Oh, not good.

197
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,940
Hold the rep, hurry up!

198
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:41,520
Pull him up!

199
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,280
Let's go!

200
00:24:25,460 --> 00:24:26,560
This isn't good.

201
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:29,600
Yes, we cannot get out of the truck.

202
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:38,627
Bastard, how dare you
do something like this?

203
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:42,740
I'm starting up the truck what

204
00:24:45,120 --> 00:24:45,950
Mr.

205
00:24:46,033 --> 00:24:47,897
Joestar, don't tell me
you're running away?

206
00:24:47,980 --> 00:24:51,880
For now, the priority is to
get away from that stand.

207
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:08,980
Let's go.

208
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,960
The escape by truck.

209
00:25:51,100 --> 00:25:55,820
Evidently, they know now that I and Duel
can detect even the slightest sound.

210
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:59,960
Although knowing that fact isn't
going to help them too much.

211
00:26:12,060 --> 00:26:15,060
Since our enemy seems to
move by detecting sound,

212
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:18,617
it can move throughout the sand
without exposing itself to us.

213
00:26:18,700 --> 00:26:22,497
It can attack us from any direction
before we even notice it's there.

214
00:26:22,580 --> 00:26:26,237
And what's worse, the main body
doesn't have to be anywhere near it.

215
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:28,420
How's Kakyoin doing? It's bad.

216
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:30,100
He could lose his sight.

217
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,341
We've got to get him to a doctor.

218
00:26:49,100 --> 00:26:49,930
Polnareff!

219
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:52,360
What's that?

220
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:02,140
There is water in the club?

221
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:06,677
The dog it escaped from the truck before

222
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:11,337
my attack began that could be a problem?

223
00:27:11,420 --> 00:27:13,820
But I'll take care of it later.

224
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:17,240
Slow down the truck!

225
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:25,520
Hold the rest.

226
00:27:30,220 --> 00:27:31,050
Chariots.

227
00:27:45,460 --> 00:27:46,640
You asshole!

228
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:49,273
I'm gonna jump you into pieces this way!

229
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:50,310
Pull around!

230
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:56,460
You like that?

231
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,750
Huh?

232
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:04,817
What the...

233
00:28:04,900 --> 00:28:07,680
what's going on with this... thing?

234
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:14,740
It combined with more water.

235
00:28:15,220 --> 00:28:16,580
This is very bad.

236
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:18,059
He will suffocate.

237
00:28:30,260 --> 00:28:31,880
Please stand back.

238
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:39,940
Magicians, red!

239
00:28:47,740 --> 00:28:48,940
Red boys!

240
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:56,469
Ballarat, spit the
water outside the truck.

241
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,840
Are you all right?

242
00:29:10,020 --> 00:29:11,677
What do you think we should do now?

243
00:29:11,760 --> 00:29:14,878
Unless we find the enemy's
main body, we're finished.

244
00:29:22,180 --> 00:29:24,900
Old man, the water and the radiator. Shit.

245
00:29:45,940 --> 00:29:47,340
Oh!

246
00:29:53,600 --> 00:29:54,430
Huh?

247
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:08,510
Oh!

248
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:46,620
No one, move!

249
00:30:49,380 --> 00:30:51,240
Do not make a sound.

250
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:01,337
I know where each one of you landed.

251
00:31:01,420 --> 00:31:03,977
And with the precision of a surgeon!

252
00:31:04,060 --> 00:31:05,657
I shall take you out.

253
00:31:05,740 --> 00:31:07,580
One by one.

254
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:13,517
What a pain!

255
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:16,660
This is a very tough stand to fight?

256
00:31:18,740 --> 00:31:19,570
But

257
00:31:26,780 --> 00:31:29,380
This is getting pretty interesting.

258
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:02,820
Vincero.

259
00:32:10,560 --> 00:32:11,960
Vincero.

260
00:32:15,820 --> 00:32:21,960
I love you, I love you.

261
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:49,420
Thank you.

262
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:50,730
Thank you.

263
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:15,420
Thank you.

264
00:34:44,460 --> 00:34:45,980
Is Is Is

265
00:34:48,160 --> 00:34:50,000
Is Is Is

266
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:53,440
Thank you.
